Day 53/100 of #DrGVishwanathanChallenge
Today, I solved LeetCode 101-(Symmetric Tree)
-Problem :
Given the root of a binary tree determine whether the tree is a mirror image of itself i.e symmetric around its center.

-Approach : Mirror Reflection
The key idea is to compare the left and right subtrees simultaneously.
For every pair of nodes:
If both nodes are null -> they are symmetric.
If only one node is null -> not symmetric.
If their values are different -> not symmetric.
Otherwise, recursively compare:
Left child of the left subtree <-> Right child of the right subtree
Right child of the left subtree <-> Left child of the right subtree
This recursive mirror comparison makes the solution simple and avoids unnecessary traversal logic.

Time Complexity: O(n)
Each node is visited once.
Space Complexity: O(h)
Due to the recursion stack, where h is the height of the tree. In the worst case, it can be O(n).

-Key Takeaway
1) Today's problem reinforced an important concept in Binary Trees and Recursion
2) Sometimes, instead of checking a structure directly, comparing two parts as mirror images can make the solution much simpler.
